  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who hold reactionary or conservative views that favor traditional societal norms and perceive contemporary expressions of Black femininity as morally or aesthetically inferior. The meme appeals to those who use historical comparisons to judge modern culture, particularly those who believe that societal standards were 'better' in the past (e.g., 1947). It is designed to resonate with audiences who may be uncomfortable with or critical of modern Black female fashion and body autonomy, and who may be influenced by or reinforce anti-Black hypersexualization stereotypes. The meme's format and text are crafted to provoke agreement from those who view the 2017 image as 'terribly right' in a negative sense, thereby validating their existing biases.",
